  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Provençale is a 4-star campsite in Mandelieu-la-Napoule, between Cannes and the Estérel massif. Its official website describes a green setting with air-conditioned mobile homes, chalets with 1 to 3 bedrooms and pitches for tents, caravans and motorhomes, plus a heated pool with a slide and a guinguette restaurant. The tourist office places the beaches about 3 km away.</p>

      <h2>Conditions for your dog</h2>
      <p>The campsite website states that animals are accepted, except 1st and 2nd category dogs and exotic pets, with one dog per rental. The rentals page specifies "one dog per rental (under 6 kg, small dog)", so a large dog is not planned for in a mobile home or chalet. The page does not say whether the weight limit also applies to pitches.</p>
      <p>The amount of any surcharge is not published by the campsite. A listing from the reseller Maeva mentions €28 per stay, with the dog vaccinated and on a lead, but this figure does not appear on the official website.</p>
      <div class="callout">Worth checking before you book: the surcharge for your dog, and the 6 kg limit if you come with a pitch. The campsite can be reached on 04 92 97 23 92 or by email.</div>

      <h2>Practical</h2>
      <p>The campsite is announced open from 26 March to 6 November 2027. Reception is open 8:30 am to 12 pm and 2 pm to 6 pm in April, May, June and September, 8 am to 12 pm and 2 pm to 7 pm in July and August, 9 am to 12 pm and 2 pm to 6 pm in October and November. In high season, rental arrivals are on Wednesday, Saturday and Sunday for a minimum of 7 nights; outside high season, rentals start at 2 nights.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Estérel massif, close by, offers walks among red rocks and pines. Cannes is a few kilometres away and Nice about 30 km.</p>
